; pcrec VM program listing (DD-8; docs/design/engine_m4.md S10)
;
; Produced BY the emitter's own walk, not by a second walk over the
; AST: every line below was written by the same call that wrote the
; corresponding C. S10's one constraint -- "the dump must be derived
; from the same structure the emitter walks, never a parallel
; description" -- is therefore structural here, not a discipline.
;
; pattern      ((a)|b)+c
; engine       vm (forced by: capture group at pattern offset 0)
; prefilter    NO (--engine=vm) -- the VM scans from search_from itself (R21 E-6)
; rungs        revdet -- see the RUNGS section below for which quantifier took which
; strategies   possessive -- see the STRATEGIES section below for which quantifier took which
; possessify   1 of 1 source quantifier possessified (eng_brep_design.md S2)
; caps         RX_NCAPS 3 (2 capturing groups in the pattern text)
; step budget  500000000 backtrack resumptions
; capacities   3 resume frames, 8 trail entries (exact: no subject ceiling)
; program      26 labels, 73 events
; resume pts   2
; max replicas 0 (limit 64, checked before emission)

SLOTS (the slot_values array, engine_m4.md S2.4)
  slot         holds                  note
   0,1         $0 whole match         written by the ENTRY, not the VM (S3.4)
   2,3         group 1                written on traverse, trailed
   4,5         group 2                written on traverse, trailed
  (no empty-iteration guard slots: no nullable unbounded quantifier on the frames rung)
  (no span-loop low-water slots: no cursor rung in this program)
  6            revdet loop entry      the capture walk's floor (S2.5)
  7            revdet low-water       boundary after rmin iterations: the retreat's floor
  8            revdet ceiling         maximal boundary reached: the lazy extension's cap

RUNGS (engine_m4.md S2.5; D46's per-quantifier stamp)
  at L0      revdet             reverse-deterministic rung {1,}, greedy, POSSESSIFIED -- ONE body copy, no replication

STRATEGIES (eng_brep_design.md S2; D47.3's per-quantifier stamp)
  at L0      possessive     reverse-deterministic rung {1,}, greedy, POSSESSIFIED -- ONE body copy, no replication

PRUNING (k23_design.md; D51's per-quantifier stamp)
  ceiling: the subject end -- either no prefilter, or the prefilter's window END is not a bound on this match's end: the pattern carries an ATOMIC GROUP (atomic_groups_design.md 4.4 H3) or a LOOKAROUND (lookaround_design.md 5.6), or the prefilter was built from the COUNT-COLLAPSED superset (prefilter_count_independence.md 2 H3, K39/[OPT-4]) -- the `; prefilter` line above says which
  bound sites emitted: 1
  runtime-term length retreats: 0
  at L0      clamped      reverse-deterministic rung {1,}, greedy, POSSESSIFIED -- ONE body copy, no replication

PROGRAM
  L0      ; reverse-deterministic rung {1,}, greedy, POSSESSIFIED -- ONE body copy, no replication
         set     slot_values[6] <- scan_position ; revdet: the loop's entry position (the capture walk's floor)
         -> L3
  L3      ; revdet scan: try one more iteration
         ; MRL: no room for another iteration and the follow -- stop the scan on the boundary it is standing on
         PUSH    resume L6                    ; this iteration cannot run -- leave the loop with the ones that did
         -> L4
  L4      ; group 1 opens
         -> L13
  L13     ; alternation entry (2 branches)
         PUSH    resume L17                   ; branch 1 of 2 preferred; resume tries branch 2
         -> L15
  L17     ; alternation resume: try branch 2 of 2
         -> L16
  L15     ; group 2 opens
         -> L18
  L18
         consume 'a'                          -> L19
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L19     ; group 2 closes
         -> L14
  L16
         consume 'b'                          -> L14
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L14     ; group 1 closes
         -> L5
  L5      ; revdet scan: one iteration committed
         ; work charge: frames discarded by the revdet scan cut
         ; cut to the iteration's entry depth: a unique-iteration body has no second parse of what just matched
         set     slot_values[7] <- scan_position ; revdet: low-water = the boundary after rmin iterations
         -> L3
  L6      ; revdet scan: the body could not run at this boundary
         -> L7
  L7      ; revdet: the forward scan is complete
         set     slot_values[8] <- scan_position ; revdet: the maximal boundary reached (the lazy extension's ceiling)
         -> L8
  L8      ; revdet: commit at this boundary
         -> L9
  L9      ; revdet walk: one step back over the committed span
         -> L10
  L10     ; group 1: its END, met first going backward
         -> L20
  L20     ; backward alternation (2 branches): the byte selects, no frame
         -> L12
  L22     ; group 2: its END, met first going backward
         -> L24
  L24
         consume 'a'                          -> L25
         -> L12
  L25     ; group 2: its START -- the last iteration that entered it wins
         -> L21
  L23
         consume 'b'                          -> L21
         -> L12
  L21     ; group 1: its START -- the last iteration that entered it wins
         -> L11
  L11     ; revdet walk: landed on the previous boundary
         -> L9
  L12     ; revdet walk: done (all groups witnessed, or the loop's entry reached)
         set     slot_values[2] <- scan_position ; group 1 open, recovered by the backward walk
         set     slot_values[3] <- scan_position ; group 1 close, recovered by the backward walk
         set     slot_values[4] <- scan_position ; group 2 open, recovered by the backward walk
         set     slot_values[5] <- scan_position ; group 2 close, recovered by the backward walk
         ; a group the walk never witnessed keeps its previous value -- which is §3.4's ZERO-ITERATION clause at the boundary where the loop never ran
         -> L2
  L2
         consume 'c'                          -> L1
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L1      ; the pattern is complete
         -> accept
  accept   ; return scan_position - ctx->pos; the capture slots at this instant ARE the answer (S3.1)
  fail     ; the ONLY backtracker and the only indirect jump; one step charged here (S4.2)

CHOICE POINTS (preference order: the frame pushed at a site resumes the LESS preferred alternative)
  at L3      resume L6      this iteration cannot run -- leave the loop with the ones that did
  at L13     resume L17     branch 1 of 2 preferred; resume tries branch 2

DFA ISLANDS (0)
  (none: no flat alternation in this program has a finite literal language, so src/gen/emit_vm.c's alternation island declined every one -- docs/spec/tuning.md S2.20)

CALLOUT SITES (0)
  (none: module 'callouts' has no producer, so no pattern can reach a call site -- engine_m4.md S9.1)
